<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Darß Weststrand–Darßer Ort circuit — Darß Weststrand–Darßer Ort circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start at the Nordstrand tourist-information approach in Prerow, walk through the village and Darß forest via Alter Grenzstein and Mittelweg to the Weststrand, and follow the full beach course north to Darßer Ort and the lighthouse/NATUREUM approach. Continue through the Darßer Ort observation circuit and return along the Nordstrand and existing approaches to the same starting ground. The long Weststrand section is part of this itinerary.

Use the existing walking course and the controlled bare-beach corridor; stay out of dunes, cliffs, closed areas and sensitive vegetation. In the National Park core zone keep to designated ways and follow signs and Ranger instructions. Coastal erosion, fallen trees, high water, storms and temporary wildlife or maintenance closures can make a required section unavailable. Do not force passage or create a dune bypass; if the full course is closed or impassable, this exact itinerary is unavailable. The flat route includes tiring soft sand. Plan for daylight and suitable weather in spring, summer or autumn, carry a map, keep dogs leashed and take rubbish home.

The complete captured OpenStreetMap path is approximately 17.5 km; allow about five hours. The inherited 6 m ascent and descent are approximate estimates, not a surveyed elevation profile. Geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0. This is a descriptive planning route with no elevation data; it is not navigation-grade. Lighthouse or museum admission and opening hours are separate from walking access.

